hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"141","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Juhni said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah, some riders appeared. When we saw them, he said: ""These are the people of Muzayjijah."" Then some men from Muzayjijah came. He said: ""I will go to them to make a covenant with them."" He took hold of one of them and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! See who has come to see you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you. What is his reward?"" He said: ""For him is forgiveness."" He then patted him on the hand and turned away. Then another man came, and he took hold of him, saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! See who has come to see you, believed in you, confirmed you, and followed you, but did not see you."" He said: ""For him is forgiveness, then for him is forgiveness, then for him is forgiveness."" He then patted him on the hand and turned away."
"142","Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr said, on the authority of his father: We sat with al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him) one day, when a man passed by and said, ""Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family)! By Allah, we wish we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed."" At this al-Miqdad became angry, and I was astonished, for the man had said nothing but good. Then he turned to the man and said: ""What leads a man to wish for a scene that Allah kept him away from, when he does not know how he would have fared had he been present in it? By Allah, there were people present with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) whom Allah cast down on their faces into Hell, for they did not answer him or believe him. Do you not thank Allah that when He brought you forth, you knew none but your Lord, believing in what your Prophet brought, and you were spared the trial that befell others? By Allah, Allah sent the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) at the harshest of times at which a prophet had ever been sent among the prophets, a time of spiritual dearth and ignorance, when people believed no religion was better than the worship of idols. Then he came with a criterion (Furqan) by which he distinguished between truth and falsehood, and separated a father from his son, such that a man might see his father, his son, and his brother as disbelievers, while Allah had opened the lock of his own heart to faith; he knew that if he died in disbelief, that man would enter the Fire, and his eye would never find rest, knowing his beloved was in the Fire. That is what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, referred to when He said: 'Those who say: Our Lord, grant us from among our spouses and offspring comfort to our eyes' [Surah al-Furqan: 74]."""
"143","From Abu Hurairah, who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) ordered Bilal to announce to the people that none would enter Paradise except a Muslim."
"144","I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah about the battle in which a man was killed, and a dog was sent to announce it to the people. He said, ""We were at Hunayn, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, ordered a man to announce it to the people, saying, 'It is not for one who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day to enter Paradise.'"""""
"145","I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah about the battle in which a man was killed, and a dog was sent to announce it to the people. He said, ""We were at Hunayn, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, ordered a man to announce it to the people, saying, 'It is not for one who does not believe in Allah and the Last Day to enter Paradise.'"""""
"146","I asked Jabir b. 'Abd Allah about the battle in which a man was killed, and a dog was sent to announce it to the people. He said, ""We were at Hunayn, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) sent a dog to announce it to the people, saying, 'It will not enter Paradise except for a believer.'"""""
"147","The believers in this world are three types: those who believe in Allah and His Messenger, then do not waver and strive with their wealth and lives in the way of Allah, and those who are wronged by people in their wealth and lives, then those who, when they look at something, abandon it for the sake of Allah, the Exalted."
"148","The believer is generous and noble, and the wicked is miserly and ignoble."
"149","And from him, 'Ayadh, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Allah, the Exalted, said: 'The believer is with me in the rank of every good, he praises me and I am pleased with his soul from between his two sides.'"""" 150,The believer will be tested by his/her devils just as a traveler is tested by his/her baggage."
"150","[AI-translation] And from him in another narration, that the Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed, the believer wears out his devils just as one of you wears out his camel on a journey."" (Musnad Ahmad: 8927)"
"151","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I will inform you of the believer, the one whom people have entrusted with their properties and their lives, and the Muslim, the one who is at peace with the Muslims from his tongue and hand, and the mujahid, the one who has fought for his soul in the obedience of Allah, and the migrant, the one who has fled from the abominations and sins."""""
"152","Musa ibn Ali said: I heard my father say, I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-'As say, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""Do you know who the Muslim is?"" They said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand other Muslims are safe."" He said, ""Do you know who the believer is?"" They said, ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The believer is he whom the believers trust with their lives and their wealth, and the emigrant (Muhajir) is one who abandons evil and avoids it."""
"153","Musa bin Ali said, ""I heard my father say, 'I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As say, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say, ""Do you know what the Muslim is?"" They said, ""God and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The Muslim is he whose tongue and hand are pure."" He said, ""Do you know who the believer is?"" They said, ""God and His Messenger know best."" He said, ""The believer is he who believes in Allah and His Messenger, and who migrates for the sake of Allah, and who flees from what Allah has forbidden.'"""""
"154","The faithful believer is one who is filled with faith, and there is no good in one who is not filled with faith and is not filled with it."
"155","From Abu Umama, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) took my hand and said to me: ""O Abu Umama, indeed among the believers is one who will be pleased with his heart."""""
"156","A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I have memorized the Quran, but I do not find my heart at peace with it."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, ""Indeed, your heart has been sealed with faith, and indeed faith is given to the servant before the Quran."""""
"157","A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, I am going to narrate to myself a hadith, and if I reach the heavens, I will be more eager to do so than if I were to speak with it."""""
"158","And from him, on another occasion, they said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We find in ourselves what pleases us, we talk about it, and we have something that the sun has risen over it."" He said: ""Have you found that?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""That is the freshness of faith."""""
"159","And even more so, I heard from my father that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you will say to the grape, 'This is the vineyard,' for indeed the vineyard is the Muslim man."""""
"160","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""They will say, 'The grape', and indeed the grape is the heart of the believer."""""
"161","By the One Who is with me, the example of a believer is like a piece of gold that has been blown upon by its owner, so it does not change or decrease. By the One Who is with me, the example of a believer is like a gazelle that has eaten good and clean food, and has stored it, and has given birth, so it does not break or spoil."
"162","The example of a believer is like that of a sprout of grass, which comes out in the morning and dries up in the evening, and the example of a disbeliever is like that of a dry tree stump, which remains dry until it is cut down."
"163","The example of a believer is like that of a horse that is ridden, then it returns to its original state. And indeed, the believer is ridden, then he returns to his faith."
"164","The Islam is a means, it does not ride except on a means."
"165","I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Faith will become strange and will return as it began. Good luck on that day to the people of the evening when time is corrupted. And that which my father's portion is in his hand will surely be divided between these two mosques, just as the living creature is divided in its womb."""""
